---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="John D. Williams — film graduate, cybersecurity MBA, SpaceX engineer, nature photographer. Liberal arts meets technology."
>
  <!-- HERO — Portrait with full-bleed image -->
  <section class="relative py-16 md:py-24 overflow-hidden">
    <img
      src="/images/photography/hero/john-portrait-bw.webp"
      alt=""
      class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-top opacity-15"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-[#0a0a0a] via-[#0a0a0a]/80 to-transparent"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 container-narrow">
      <div class="reveal max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase opacity-30 mb-4 font-light">About</p>
        <h1 class="mb-8">About</h1>
        <p class="text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed opacity-70">
          I studied film. I work in cybersecurity. I shoot landscapes with a Sony A7R
          and build data pipelines in Python. The through-line is not obvious until you
          see it: I have always been interested in how things are made visible — whether
          that is a story on screen, a threat on a network, or light on a mountain.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BACKGROUND — alternating section -->
  <section class="section-light py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="reveal prose max-w-2xl">
        <h2>Background</h2>
        <p>
          I graduated from Baylor University in 2015 with a BA in Film and Digital Media.
          That degree taught me composition, narrative structure, and how to communicate
          visually — skills I still use daily, just in different contexts. I went to law
          school. Life intervened. I left, earned an MBA in Cybersecurity from
          Baylor and Texas A&amp;M University-Corpus Christi (2024, 3.86 GPA), and found
          that the analytical rigor of security work suited me better than the courtroom
          ever would have.
        </p>
        <p>
          For the past two years I have worked at SpaceX on the Starlink enterprise
          support team, running night shift operations. That means incident command across
          enterprise, government, aviation, and maritime accounts — 175+ P1/P2 incidents
          per week, building forecasting tools from scratch, and designing operational
          analytics in an environment where downtime is not abstract.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE INTERSECTION -->
  <section class="relative py-16 md:py-24 overflow-hidden">
    <img
      src="/images/photography/gallery/7r52258.webp"
      alt=""
      class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-1/3 h-full object-cover opacity-10 hidden lg:block"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="reveal prose max-w-2xl">
        <h2>The Intersection</h2>
        <p>
          People ask why a film graduate ended up in cybersecurity and data engineering.
          The honest answer is that I never left the core discipline. Film is about
          taking raw material — footage, sound, light — and organizing it so that someone
          else can see what you see. Data engineering is the same problem with different
          inputs. Cybersecurity is about making the invisible visible before it causes
          damage. Photography is about noticing what is already there.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work at the intersection of these things because that is where I actually
          live. The liberal arts and technology are not separate tracks for me. They are
          the same track, and the best work I do happens when both are engaged.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT I AM BUILDING — alternating -->
  <section class="section-light py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="reveal prose max-w-2xl">
        <h2>What I Am Building</h2>
        <p>
          Outside of SpaceX, I am building Noticing — a venture with three arms.
          Noticing Solutions handles AI and technology consulting. Noticing Nature is
          my photography practice: landscape and nature work, shot on a Sony A7R system,
          with nearly 3,000 images in the archive and print sales on the way. Noticing
          Scripture is a faith-based content project structured as a nonprofit.
        </p>
        <p>
          The name comes from a conviction: most of what matters is already in front of
          us. The work is learning to see it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CREDENTIALS -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="reveal prose max-w-2xl">
        <h2>Credentials</h2>
        <p>
          BA in Film and Digital Media, Baylor University (2015). MBA in Cybersecurity,
          Baylor / Texas A&amp;M University-Corpus Christi (2024, 3.86 GPA). Eagle Scout.
          ITAR clearance. CompTIA Security+ (in progress). I am also pursuing an Air Force
          Reserve commission in cybersecurity operations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OUTSIDE WORK — alternating, with image grid -->
  <section class="section-light py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="reveal prose max-w-2xl mb-12">
        <h2>Outside Work</h2>
        <p>
          I am a nature photographer. That is not a hobby line on a resume — it is a
          real practice with commercial intent, and it feeds everything else I do. I am
          a person of faith. I am an Eagle Scout. I believe in service, in showing up when
          it is hard, and in doing the work that is in front of you without waiting for
          applause.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
        <div class="rounded-card overflow-hidden aspect-[3/4] ring-1 ring-white/6">
          <img src="/images/photography/gallery/img-7055-enhanced-enhanced-sr.webp" alt="Sunset over wildflower field" class="w-full h-full object-cover" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-card overflow-hidden aspect-[3/4] ring-1 ring-white/6">
          <img src="/images/photography/gallery/dscf0936.webp" alt="Mountain landscape with clouds" class="w-full h-full object-cover" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-card overflow-hidden aspect-[3/4] ring-1 ring-white/6">
          <img src="/images/photography/gallery/7r51108-enhanced-sr.webp" alt="Sunlight through tree canopy" class="w-full h-full object-cover" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="reveal glass-card p-10 max-w-lg">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif mb-4">Work together?</h2>
        <p class="opacity-50 mb-8">
          I take on select consulting work in data engineering, cybersecurity
          operations, and technical strategy.
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:hello@thejohndwilliams.com" class="btn btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
